    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Profile : {{ $('Filter: Keep Only Valid Emails').item.json.person_full_name }}\nCompany Name : {{ $('Scrape: Google Maps Leads (Apify)').item.json.title }}\nWebScraper :  {{ $json.text }}",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "You will take summaries and turn them into cold-email icebreakers and full emails that feel tight, specific, and quietly personal—just enough to signal that the rest of the message is tailored for the Indian business context.\n\nUse this exact flow and structure for the email_body:\n\nHey {name}. Love {interesting_fact}—also doing/like/a fan of {otherFact}. Wanted to run something by you.\n\nI hope you'll forgive me, but I went through your site quite a bit, and know that {otherFact} is important to you guys (or at least I'm assuming this given the focus on {fourthFact}). I put something together a few months ago that I think could help. To make a long story short, it's an outreach system that uses AI to find people hiring website devs. Then pitches them with templates (actually makes them a demo website). Costs just a few rupees to run, very high converting, and I think it's in line with {someImpliedBeliefTheyHave}.\n\nWorth a quick chat, or should I send over a short video showing how it works?\n\nBest,\n[Your Name]\n\nRules:\n- Keep the tone sparse, dry, and to-the-point.\n- Shorten company names whenever possible (“Infosys” instead of “Infosys Limited”, “TCS” instead of “Tata Consultancy Services”).\n- Same idea with locations (“Bangalore” instead of “Bengaluru Urban”, “Delhi” instead of “New Delhi”, “Mumbai” instead of “Mumbai Metropolitan Region”).\n- For variables, pull out small, specific details—not the obvious stuff. No generic compliments. Aim for details that look hand-picked from deep browsing."
        }
      },
